Z||000000||AusFiero||06-21-2001||11:26 AM||||Well a forum member asked me via email to try find a certain style of wheel for them. Which I did recognise straight away luckily as an Aussie one.<P>Are these worth putting on <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>www.auto-alley.com</A>  with my sub boxes and stuff ?<P>I spoke to the manufacturer today and although they are not normally made to suit our cars they can custom make them for me. They are, well can be, 15X7 or 15X8 with a 5X100 bolt pattern with a 34mm offset.<P>They would cost US $225 a rim which includes delivery to USA or Canada and full insurance. <BR>Worth it, or scrap it, bearing in mind they are custom made ?  <P>The silver and gold ones are editted photoshop versions as I only had a picture of the black.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/globesilver.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/globegold.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/globeblack.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jaygee79||06-21-2001||11:38 AM||||I like the black ones.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Formula88||06-21-2001||11:43 AM||||I really like them, but I wouldn't spend the money on them for just 15".  If they were 16" or 17" for about $225ea, I'd be interested.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Steven||06-21-2001||11:49 AM||||To me they kind of look dated. But if you like them, thats all that counts.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||06-21-2001||12:08 PM||||no offence but i think it is ugly, but we all have our opinions... I went to my local rice store yesturday, saw a set of Konig monsoon's MO Series... they guy that was working didnt no much about they like what bolt patterns and stuff... they are offered from 15"-18" 5 spokes...   for the 15 x 6.5 are 166.95  nice looking all try to find a pic<P>If i go back today what should the offset be? (I want a pair of 17's or 16's)  i'll take pix if i go also<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||06-21-2001||12:15 PM||||Konig Monsoons come in just about every bolt pattern and offset immaginable. There is a set that will fit your Fiero. The guy at the "rice shop" should be able to look your car up in the book and see what size will fit. If he can't do that then I wouldn't buy from him. Monsoons are available at Discount/Americas Tire if you have one in your are for very cheap. If not almost any tire shop can order them. You can look up the correct size for your car online at <A HREF="http://www.tires.com" TARGET=_blank>www.tires.com</A>  and buy them online if you want.||||reg||1
Z||000006||KRMFiero||06-21-2001||12:20 PM||||Hmm thanks, I just called town fair tire, they said it is avaliable for the 5x100 bolt pattern, for the 17x7's it is $210.81  not to bad, here is a pic:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/monsoon.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||06-21-2001||12:44 PM||||Mixed views as I expected. Personally they are not my choice either but thats what I was asked for. Each wheel to each car and application and owner etc.<P>Pricewise they seem fair then as I too could supply 17"s for around the $210 shown and still include delivery. These rims would be custom made so that always makes a difference. They can also be $15 a rim cheaper by using a slower shipping method.<P>Will look around at what 17"s are available. here that aren't available there. Quality ones only though, not cheap and nasties. <P>Quality being type and grade of alloy used and finish.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 06-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||pherder||06-21-2001||01:01 PM||||AusFiero,<P>I bet the person that asked for them was looking to put them on a rebodied Fiero (308/328) since they are the closest to being a match for the stock Ferrari 308/328 wheels.<P>In the early 90s, I got a set of those wheels, made in Austriala, shipped to Canada and then purchased by me here in the US.<P>I had both sizes (7s up front and the 8s on the rear) of my 308 kit.  They came stock in black and I had them stripped and powdered coated silver.  Made the kit look good.<P>I spent a lot less than the $225 each but it is good they are still available for the 308/328 crowd.<P>BTW, the 8" will stick out quite a ways on the rear of a stock Fiero.  My 308 kit was 3" wider on each side @ the rear and those wheels (with 245R5015 Euro TA tires) fit under the fenders just about exactly!<P>Paul<BR>308 sold - Artero in progress||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||06-21-2001||01:33 PM||||Ahhh for the prices of the early 90s Pherder  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>But on another note:<BR>Ok I did a quick bit of research on what I can get hold of do these sound better? Cheaper because they are not custom made.<P>16X7" mags from $150 - 17X7" or  8" from $175 - 18X7" or 8" from $199 - 19X7" or 8" from $220 - 17X7" or 8" Chrome Alloys from $199. All price would still include delivery and insurance.<P>Will get some pictures of different styles and more exct pricing on the different styles if there is enough interest. ||||reg||5
